––– comment –––
Single-filter COUNT(*) has a separate precalculation path. For each bound print the
unhinted count and the NO_SecondaryIndex count; both must use the ordered comparison.
––– input –––
for attr in rs cs; do
  for bound in m ''; do
    for op in '<' '<=' '>' '>='; do
      printf "%s %s '%s': " "$attr" "$op" "$bound"
      sql "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM gh5006 WHERE $attr $op '$bound'; SELECT COUNT(*) FROM gh5006 WHERE $attr $op '$bound' /*+ NO_SecondaryIndex($attr) */;" | paste -sd, -
    done
  done
done
